meta {
  name: xyops - create template
  type: http
  seq: 24
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "template_id": "xyops",
    "description": "xyOps - workflow automation + server monitoring (pixlcore/xyops). Self-contained (SQLite + filesystem, no external DB).",
    "metatags": [
      "xyops",
      "workflow",
      "automation",
      "monitoring",
      "ops",
      "http"
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  ## Create the `xyops` template
  
  Run this once before the tags below. xyOps (https://github.com/pixlcore/xyops) is a Node-based
  "workflow automation and server monitoring system" from PixlCore (the Cronicle authors).
  
  > ⚠️ **No published image yet.** As of authoring, xyOps has **no official container image**
  > (GitHub Packages: 0; not on Docker Hub). You must **build it from the repo Dockerfile**, push
  > it to a registry the Pods service can pull, and **add it to the Pods image allowlist**. The tags
  > below use `pixlcore/xyops:latest` as a placeholder — change it to your built image.
  >
  > ```bash
  > git clone https://github.com/pixlcore/xyops && cd xyops
  > docker build -t <your-registry>/xyops:latest .
  > docker push <your-registry>/xyops:latest
  > ```
}
